============================================================================
EMP DETECTION DEPTH: a degree-d charge-0 polynomial B(s) survives EXACTLY d moments
============================================================================
 B monic degree d (d free coeffs).  survival = max k with a nonzero B killing L(B^1..k).
 depth = survival+1.  Claim: survival = d, depth = d+1.

  d=1: survival = 1  (depth = 2)   -> survival==d: True
  d=2: survival = 2  (depth = 3)   -> survival==d: True
  d=3: survival = 3  (depth = 4)   -> survival==d: True
  d=4: survival = 4  (depth = 5)   -> survival==d: True

 => EMP DETECTION DEPTH = d+1, exactly.  Since a GMC(2) P may contain a degree-d charge-0 part,
 the GMC(2) detection depth is >= d+1 for EVERY radial degree d -- an UNCONDITIONAL, PROVEN floor
 that grows linearly with degree.  This upgrades THM-1770's single d=1 witness to a proven law:
 the detection depth is not merely 'not span-only', it is bounded BELOW by the radial degree.
 The analytic bridge must dominate resonance of order >= d+1 at radial degree d -- no finite,
 degree-uniform elimination can, because EMP alone already forces depth -> infinity with d.

